{"name":"Lucky Penny","hex":"#bc6f37","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lucky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Favoured by luck; fortunate; having good success or good fortune.","Producing, or resulting in, good fortune"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["seven"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lucky"},{"term":"penny","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In the United Kingdom and Ireland and many other countries, a unit of currency worth ⁄240 of a pound sterling or Irish pound before decimalisation, or a copper coin worth this amount. Abbreviation: d.","In the United Kingdom, a unit of currency worth ⁄100 of a pound sterling, or a copper coin worth this amount. Abbreviation: p."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To jam a door shut by inserting pennies between the doorframe and the door.","To circumvent the tripping of an electrical circuit breaker by the dangerous practice of inserting a coin in place of a fuse in a fuse socket."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/penny"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lucky Penny","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lucky Penny\" is the 15th episode in the second season of the television series How I Met Your Mother and 37th overall. It originally aired on CBS on February 12, 2007."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucky_Penny","wikidata":"Q6697995"},{"title":"Penny","blocks":[{"text":"A penny is a coin or a unit of currency in various countries. Borrowed from the Carolingian denarius, it is usually the smallest denomination within a currency system. At present, it is the formal name of the British penny unit and the de facto name of the American one-cent coin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/1911-Australian-Penny-Reverse.jpg/330px-1911-Australian-Penny-Reverse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Penny","wikidata":"Q234129"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.